From 70593af6e38b0b4fdbf2b13454b8a9860538b395 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:49:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a configurable Quick Add shortcut button to the Home
 Dashboard and Site Blocks headers

Settings > Quick Add gets two independent type pickers -- Home
Dashboard and Site Blocks page can each be configured with their own
block type, defaulting to "None" -- since a deployment might mostly
create one type of block on one page and a different type on the
other. There's no separate enable switch: a page's button appears as
soon as that page's picker is set to anything other than "None", and
disappears again if it's reset back to "None". When shown, the button
is styled with that type's color and icon (matching the existing
type_color()-driven styling used elsewhere) and jumps straight to
main.new_block for that type, skipping the "New Site Block" modal's
type picker.

- configstore.py: get_quick_add_type_dashboard()/
  get_quick_add_type_site_blocks(), each validated against
  QUICK_ADD_BLOCK_TYPES, falling back to None on anything else.
- views.py: dashboard()/site_blocks() pass their own page's configured
  type; settings() gains an update_quick_add POST action, rejecting
  any block type value outside the known set.
- templates/partials/quick_add_button.html: new shared partial (same
  "one partial, included by both pages" pattern as new_block_modal.html)
  that renders the button only when a type is set, mirroring the
  icon/label/color used by the existing type-picker modal.
- settings.html: real Quick Add tab (was a lorem-ipsum stub) with the
  two <select> pickers, both visible directly -- no toggle to show/hide
  them first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
